#import "../lib.typ": *
= Troubleshooting Checklist <ch-trouble>

The following list of symptoms, causes, and remedies is supplied to help you find the trouble when a FujiNet program does not do what you meant. Always check the status page first: `ERR` at `$B402` and `REPLYCMD` at `$B403` say most of what went wrong.

#symrem(
  ([The program never gets past its first transaction.],
   ([`'F','N'` is not at `$B409`: the image is not running from a FujiNet cartridge, or MAME was started without `-cartslot fujinet`.],
    [The image has no claim at `$BFE0`, so it runs as a GAME and the mailbox is switched off.],
    [Interrupts are off. The library’s wait counts frames by the VBI, and without it never runs out.],
    [`fujinet-pc` is not listening on the bus-over-IP port MAME was given, or another MAME is already connected to it.])),
  ([Every transaction answers with ERR 1.],
   ([There is no link to the FujiNet: the USB cable, or on the bench the adapter is not running. The cartridge waits three seconds for the link before each transaction.])),
  ([A transaction answers with ERR 2.],
   ([The FujiNet took longer than the cartridge’s budget: five seconds for most commands, sixty for a mount, ninety for the network device. Check the devicespec, the host and the server.])),
  ([A transaction answers with ERR 3.],
   ([A parameter’s size byte is not 1, 2 or 4, or NPARAM says more parameters than the TX stream holds. Count them against the command card.])),
  ([`fn_go` returns `$FF`, or C reports `FN_EWAIT`.],
   ([The cartridge never copied the sequence number: the hotspot reads went wrong. Look for a store, an `INC` or a `(zp),Y` on `$B500`–`$B7FF`, an index that crosses a page, or a loop that counts in Y round `fn_txb`.],
    [The sequence number repeated the last one. Take it from `ACKSEQ` plus one, every time.])),
  ([The FujiNet says no (`REPLYCMD` `$15`; `FNENAK` `$EE` in assembly, 144 in C).],
   ([The command was understood and refused: a host not mounted, a path that does not exist, a full appkey, a creator of 0. The card for the command lists its refusals.])),
  ([Booting another image, BOOTSTATE stays 0.],
   ([The FujiNet did not take the file for a cartridge image: it must end in `.a52` or `.bin`.],
    [The `fujinet-pc` was built before it knew `.a52`.])),
  ([Booting another image, BOOTSTATE reads `$80`.],
   ([BOOTERR 1: the image is bigger than 128K.],
    [BOOTERR 2: the file is shorter than its size said; copy it again.],
    [BOOTERR 3: no board fits it. Give it a `.cfg` file with a `mapper=` line.])),
  ([The booted program cannot find the mailbox.],
   ([It has no claim, or it is a two-chip or Bounty Bob image, which cannot be an APP (@ch-boot).])),
  ([The screen is black, or garbage.],
   ([`SDMCTL` is 0, or the display list never set: in assembly, `disp_on`; in C, `mt_init`.],
    [The display list, a screen or a font is in `$B000`–`$B7FF`, where ANTIC reads the mailbox.],
    [A screen crosses a 4K boundary, or a display list a 1K one.])),
  ([A key on the keypad acts twice.],
   ([The keypad interrupt fires on every scan of a held key. Count a key once until the hold timer has run out, as `a52init.s` and the C start-up code do.])),
  ([The stick does nothing on a real console, though it works in MAME.],
   ([`CONSOL` bit 2 is clear, so the pots are off. Write `$04` to `$C01F` (@ch-pads).])),
  ([No sound.],
   ([`SKCTL` is 0, which holds POKEY in reset; the start-up code leaves it at `$02`.],
    [The voice’s volume, the low four bits of `AUDC1`, is 0.])),
  ([A C program draws stray marks low on cc65’s console, or crashes.],
   ([The C stack is on the console’s screen: link with `__RESERVED_MEMORY__` of at least `0x1E0`.])),
  ([Text from the network comes out on one line, in C.],
   ([The code compares with `'\n'`, which cc65’s Atari targets make `$9B`. Use `0x0A` and `0x0D`.])),
  ([A Super Cart program crashes when it switches banks.],
   ([The code running at the switch, an interrupt handler, the display list or the font is not the same in every bank.],
    [Something read `$BFE0` (the claim) and selected the last bank.],
    [cc65 dropped the read that was meant to switch: do it with `BIT` in an assembly file.])),
  ([`checkrom.py` or the romstamp refuses the image.],
   ([It says what it found and where: a store or read-modify-write in the window, a hotspot read from a base that is not page-aligned, `JMP ($xxFF)`, or a missing claim or header.])),
)
